- qrcode 1.5.4 (https://github.com/soldair/node-qrcode)
  MIT License. QR symbol generation on the sender side. Its browser entry point reaches
  one runtime transitive dependency, dijkstrajs 1.0.3 (MIT).

- cbor2 2.3.0 (https://github.com/hildjj/cbor2)
  MIT License. Deterministic CBOR encoding and strict decoding. It is not a peripheral
  dependency: every wire and at-rest structure in Keyweave goes through it, including the
  signed contact card, the mailbox coordinate, the sealed envelope and the vault blob, so
  the bytes a signature covers are the bytes this library produced.

- @cto.af/wtf8 0.0.5 (https://github.com/hildjj/wtf8)
  MIT License. cbor2's sole runtime dependency, and it does ship: cbor2's encoder and its
  type table both import it at module scope, so it is not tree-shaken away, and the built
  bundle contains it. Listed separately rather than folded into the line above because an
  attribution that names only the direct dependency understates what is being distributed.

Keyweave does not stamp a blanket SPDX identifier onto built artifacts: the bundle carries
Apache-2.0 material alongside MIT, and a single MIT banner over both would misstate the
license of the decoder.
